"""Tool map, tools. Curated by hand from the sources linked in each entry (read 2026-10-16). Versions, release dates,
last commits, licences (where GitHub or PyPI state one) and the archived flag are NOT typed here: gen_data.py fills them
from inputs/ (PyPI JSON API, GitHub REST API and Atom feeds), so every dated cell has one machine-read source.
Fields: layer (hpc, k8s, orch, launch, cloud, storage, obs, flow, track), repo (GitHub), pypi (package for version and
date), relpick (regex a GitHub release title must match to count as the latest stable release, when the feed mixes in
nightlies, alphas or provider packages), lic (licence override, read from the repository's LICENSE/COPYING when GitHub
cannot detect an SPDX id, or from the vendor for closed products), status (active, maintained, maintenance, quiet,
deprecated, archived, commercial), why (the evidence for the status, one line), verdict (a judgement, labelled as such
on the page), src (sources read)."""
